{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/Se","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/SE","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/SQ","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/SH"],"kind":"relationships","type":"inheritsFrom"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Accessing boundaries","anchor":"Accessing-boundaries","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(before:)","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(after:)"]},{"title":"Accessing values","anchor":"Accessing-values","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/input(before:)","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/input(after:)"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:20FoundationEssentials19DiscreteFormatStyleP","platforms":[{"name":"iOS","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"18.0"},{"name":"iPadOS","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"18.0"},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"18.0"},{"name":"macOS","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"15.0"},{"name":"tvOS","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"18.0"},{"name":"watchOS","unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"11.0"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"protocol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DiscreteFormatStyle","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"DiscreteFormatStyle","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiscreteFormatStyle","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","modules":[{"name":"FoundationEssentials"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Data formatting","anchor":"Data-formatting","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/ParseableFormatStyle"],"generated":true}],"abstract":[{"text":"A format style that transforms a continuous input into a discrete output and provides","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"information about its discretization boundaries.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/discreteformatstyle"]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiscreteFormatStyle"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials11FormatStyleP0C5InputQa","text":"FormatInput","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/FormatInput"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials11FormatStyleP0C6OutputQa","text":"FormatOutput","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/FormatOutput"},{"kind":"text","text":"> : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials11FormatStyleP","text":"FormatStyle","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this protocol to keep displays up to date if input changes continuously, or to iterate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over all possible outputs of a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by obtaining the next discrete input in either direction"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(before:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(after:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Ordering of Inputs","anchor":"Ordering-of-Inputs","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ordering over ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/FormatInput"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"defined by ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(before:)"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(after:)"},{"text":" must be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consistent between the two functions. If ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/FormatInput"},{"text":" conforms to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"text":" protocol, the format style’s ordering ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"should","type":"text"}]},{"text":" be consistent with the canonical ordering","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"defined via the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"text":" conformance, i.e. it should hold that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"discreteInput(before: x)! < x < discreteInput(after: x)!"},{"type":"text","text":" where discrete inputs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are not nil."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Stepping through Discrete Input\/Output Pairs","level":2,"anchor":"Stepping-through-Discrete-InputOutput-Pairs","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"One use case of this protocol is enumerating all discrete inputs of a format style and their respective","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outputs.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"While the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(before:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(after:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"functions are the right tool for that, they do not give a guarantee that their respective return values","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"actually produce an output that is different from the output produced by formatting the ","type":"text"},{"code":"input","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"used when calling ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(before:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(after:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", they only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"provide a value that produces a different output for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"most","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" inputs. E.g. when formatting a floating point","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value as an integer, we can get the next discrete input after ","type":"text"},{"code":"x","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by calculating ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"floor(x + 1)"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"However, when rounding toward zero, the whole interval (-1;1) formats as zero. It would be ok for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"discrete format style to ignore that edge case and return ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(after:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"negative value greater than ","type":"text"},{"code":"-1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Therefore, to enumerate all discrete input\/output pairs, adjacent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"outputs must be deduplicated in order to guarantee no adjacent outputs are the same.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example produces all discrete input\/output pairs for inputs in a given "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"range"},{"type":"text","text":" making"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sure adjacent outputs are unequal:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension DiscreteFormatStyle","    where FormatInput : Comparable, FormatOutput : Equatable","{","        func enumerated(","        in range: ClosedRange<FormatInput>","    ) -> [(input: FormatInput, output: FormatOutput)] {","        var input = range.lowerBound","        var output = format(input)","","        var pairs = [(input: FormatInput, output: FormatOutput)]()","        pairs.append((input, output))","","        \/\/ get the next discretization bound","        while let nextInput = discreteInput(after: input),","              \/\/ check that it is still in the requested `range`","              nextInput <= range.upperBound {","            \/\/ get the respective formatted output","            let nextOutput = format(nextInput)","            \/\/ deduplicate based on the formatted output","            if nextOutput != output {","                pairs.append((nextInput, nextOutput))","            }","                input = nextInput","            output = nextOutput","        }","","        return pairs","    }","}"]},{"anchor":"Imperfect-Discretization-Boundaries","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Imperfect Discretization Boundaries"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In some scenarios, a format style cannot provide precise discretization boundaries in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a performant manner. In those cases it must override "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/input(before:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/input(after:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to reflect that. For any discretization boundary "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x"},{"type":"text","text":" returned by either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(before:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle\/discreteInput(after:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" based on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"original input ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"y"},{"text":", all values representable in the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/FormatStyle\/FormatInput","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"strictly  between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x"},{"text":" and the return value of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"input(after: x)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"input(before: x)"},{"text":", respectively, are not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"guaranteed to produce the same formatted output as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"y"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following schematic shows an overview of the guarantees given by the protocol:"}]},{"syntax":null,"code":["xB = discreteInput(before: y)       y      xA = discreteInput(after: y)","      |                             |                             |","<-----+---+-------------------------+-------------------------+---+--->","          |                                                   |"," zB = input(after: xB)                          zA = input(before: xA)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the formatted output for everything in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zB...zA"},{"type":"text","text":" (including bounds) is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"guaranteed","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to be equal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(y)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the formatted output for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xB"},{"type":"text","text":" and lower is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"most likely"}]},{"type":"text","text":" different from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(y)"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the formatted output for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xA"},{"type":"text","text":" and higher is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"most likely"}]},{"type":"text","text":" different from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(y)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the  formatted output between ","type":"text"},{"code":"xB","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"zB","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as well as ","type":"text"},{"code":"zA","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"xA","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (excluding bounds) cannot","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"be predicted","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://FoundationEssentials/documentation/FoundationEssentials/DiscreteFormatStyle":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/FoundationEssentials\/documentation\/FoundationEssentials\/DiscreteFormatStyle","type":"topic","title":"DiscreteFormatStyle","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DiscreteFormatStyle","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A format style that transforms a continuous input into a discrete output and provides","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"information about its discretization boundaries.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DiscreteFormatStyle","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/foundationessentials\/discreteformatstyle"},"doc://FoundationEssentials/Se":{"identifier":"doc:\